          "Comprehensive unit tests verify round-trip encryption/decryption parity, bit-flip sensitivity in every byte of ciphertext, AAD tampering rejection, and empty-plaintext tagging. Fuzz suites supply corrupted nonces and shortened tags to verify strict fail-closed exception handling without partial data leakage. Deterministic test fixtures confirm exact tag bytes across repeated runs under diverse Python hash seeds. Binding tenant identifiers and API schema versions into Associated Authenticated Data inside `AESGCMProtocol.encrypt` prevents ciphertext swapping attacks across database rows even when attackers control valid tenant keys. Separating random initialization vectors cleanly from fixed context labels keeps authenticated encryption capsules tamper-evident across storage migrations and multi-region blob replication pipelines. Including database table names and record primary keys inside authenticated associated data blocks row-swapping tampering cleanly across shared storage engines.",
