          "Using `AEADThroughputRouter.seal_chunked_stream`, large streams partition into sequential fixed-size segments each encrypted independently under derived per-chunk nonces and explicit sequence bindings. Combining a shared 64-bit session nonce prefix with a monotonically incrementing 32-bit chunk counter prevents cross-chunk nonce collisions automatically. Including chunk index and end-of-stream marker bits inside each segment's AAD stops active attackers from deleting, duplicating, or reordering individual stream slices.",
