          "Bounded LRU policy caches sustain enterprise API throughput without sacrificing responsiveness when permissions are revoked. Yet even fast caches encounter extreme failures—database network splits, exhausted CPU pools, or hung identity backends—forcing gateways into an existential choice between availability and security. Part 3 constructs `FailClosedCircuitBreaker` to enforce unyielding Fail-Closed resilience."
