          "Verification suites invoke `SYNFloodDetector.audit_tcp_syn_ratio` across balanced normal counts (`SYN=120, ACK=115` -> normal), spoofed heavy floods (`SYN=5000, ACK=12` -> flood detected), and low-volume zero-ACK idle samples ensuring `ZeroDivisionError` guards behave cleanly. Verified flood detection advances next to horizontal port scanning in Part 2. Comparing half-open TCP SYN ratios cleanly inside `SYNFloodDetector.audit_tcp_syn_ratio` detects resource-exhaustion denial attacks before stateful firewall connection tables overflow across internet-facing edge balancers cleanly. Checking completion-handshake deficits distinguishes true half-open SYN floods sharply away from legitimate flash-crowd user bursts carrying normal completed ACK ratios cleanly. Auditing incoming SYN-to-ACK completion ratios inside `SYNFloodDetector.audit_tcp_syn_ratio` spots asymmetric exhaustion attacks cleanly before edge load-balancers drop legitimate customer handshakes cleanly. Isolating half-open flood bursts decisively away from genuine traffic spikes keeps automated perimeter scrubbers triggering cleanly only on real handshake starvation attacks continuously. Comparing SYN handshake completion counts inside `SYNFloodDetector.audit_tcp_syn_ratio` traps volumetric half-open exhaustion bursts cleanly ahead of load-balancer saturation safely cleanly. Monitoring half-open TCP SYN ratios inside `SYNFloodDetector.audit_tcp_syn_ratio` isolates volumetric exhaustion bursts decisively away from healthy flash-crowd handshakes across internet edge routers cleanly.",
          "Tracking `SYN/ACK` parity detects volumetric connection exhaustion early, safeguarding listening endpoints against spoofed half-open storms. Long before launching noisy floods or targeted exploits, however, attackers probe public IP ranges stealthily hunting exposed SSH, database, and admin ports. Part 2 implements `HorizontalPortScanDetector` to flag reconnaissance sweeping across distinct destination ports."
