          "Inside `HorizontalPortScanDetector`, `detect_port_scans` scans incoming `flow_records` per external source IP, accumulating unique destination ports contacted inside a dictionary of Python `set` objects and flagging any source crossing `scan_port_threshold` (default `5`). Counting distinct destination ports cleanly separates heavy single-service traffic (a noisy browser opening forty connections strictly to TCP port `443`) from wide reconnaissance sweeping ports `21`, `22`, `80`, `443`, `3306`, and `6379`.",
