          "It computes the Exploitability sub-score by multiplying the weights: `Exploitability = 8.22 * AV * AC * PR * UI`.",
          "It calculates the Impact sub-score from Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability ratings, accounting for scope transitions.",
          "The combined sub-scores are summed and rounded up to the nearest single decimal place using the standard CVSS ceiling function.",
          "The calculator outputs the final numerical score (0.0 to 10.0) alongside the qualitative severity tier (Critical, High, Medium, Low).",
          "Inside `CVSSv31BaseCalculator`, `calculate_base_score` transforms exploitability attributes (`av`, `ac`, `pr`, `ui`) and `impact_level` into a quantitative Base score using official FIRST CVSS v3.1 exploitability multipliers (`8.22 * AV * AC * PR * UI`) combined with impact sub-scoring and strict one-decimal ceiling rounding (`math.ceil(score * 10) / 10`). Returning both the clamped numeric score (`<= 10.0`) and discrete severity label makes automated triage reproducible across services.",
