          "CVSS vector strings (e.g., `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`) must conform to strict grammar specifications.",
          "A malformed or truncated vector string can cause parser exceptions or result in incorrect severity calculations.",
          "The CVSS vector syntax guardrail verifies that incoming strings begin with the mandatory `CVSS:3.1/` prefix.",
          "It subsequently validates that all eight mandatory Base metrics—AV, AC, PR, UI, S, C, I, and A—are explicitly present.",
          "If any mandatory metric is missing or contains an unrecognized metric code, the guardrail rejects the vector with an informative `ValueError`.",
          "Graceful failure handling prevents corrupted security advisory feeds from disrupting automated vulnerability triage pipelines.",
